================================================================================
## Speed bulk Data Quality with a VIEW-sourced snapshot and a live log
================================================================================

Context: Knowledge Graph → Data Quality re-expanded the R2RML gateway VIEW
on every check, so a multi-rule run scanned source mappings N times.
Keep that VIEW as the only source: CTAS it once into a task-scoped Delta
table, run checks (up to 4 workers) against the copy, then drop it.
Show task.log_entries in a scrollable activity log while the run executes.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/_table_naming.py
   Add dq_snapshot_fqn(domain, settings, task_id) off the gateway stem.
2. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/quality/DataQualitySnapshot.py
   New context manager: CTAS from the VIEW, drop in finally, fall back
   to the live VIEW (sequential) if CTAS fails.
3. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/TwinBackgroundTasks.py
   Wrap the bulk DQ worker; skip snapshot when total < 2.
4. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/quality/SqlQualityChecks.py
   ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=4) only when a snapshot exists; keep
   result order; serial path unchanged for the live VIEW.
5. src/front/templates/partials/dtwin/_query_dataquality.html
   Add #dqExecProgressLog with class task-activity-log.
6. src/front/static/query/js/query-dataquality.js
   Render task.log_entries on poll (TaskProgressUI.renderActivityLog).
7. src/front/templates/dtwin.html
   Load task-progress-ui.js before query-dataquality.js.
8. tests/units/architecture/baseline.json
   Shrink-only ratchet: SqlQualityChecks.run_sql_checks left the
   oversized-function list.

